@node "About" "About SiL-WALL v2.50"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Features"}

                         - About SiL-WALL v2.50 -

 This is a simple WALL door which should be run when a user logs in
 using the MCI Launch Door command ~CC_ in for example in the BBS:Bull.txt

 Ex:

         ---------------/STARTCUT/------
         ~
         ~CC_SiLWALL
         ---------------/ENDCUT/--------
@endnode

@node "Features" "Features in SiL-WALL v2.50"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Installation"}

                        - Features in SiL-WALL v2.50 -

 This version features Relative Viewing of Quoted lines!
 That means that if a user has his NumLines set at 29 he will see
 the 22 last lines of the 100 quoted lines in the datafile.
 So if a user with Interlace or whatever and with his NumLines set
 to 60 he will see the 53 last lines of the 100 lines in the datafile!
 When the limit of 100 lines fills up it will be cut and truncated
 from the top.

 In the SilWALL.info there is a tooltype named CHEATMODE.
 The current setting is OFF. That means that if a User doesn't want
 to be anonymous his name will be printed after his quote in YELLOW
 color. That way nobody can 'cheat' and using the Anonymous option
 write another users handle in that place.
 But with CHEATMODE=ON the handles will be written the same color as
 the quotes which enables troublemakers to write shit and put another
 dudes handle in their place, can be quite amusing but if they start
 to write shit about the Sysop.. well :) you catch my drift!
 Check the 2 last quoted lines in the SiLWALL.iff picture to see
 what it looks like with or without CHEATMODE activated.
 Anyway that won't be a problem either in v3.00 wich will write the
 lines to the Callerslog, quite easy to fix but as I said, no time!!
@endnode

@node "Installation" "Installing Sil-WALL v2.50"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Package"}

                       - Installing Sil-WALL v2.50 -

 To install this put the BBSCmd icon into it's place, define
 your desirable location of the door in here. Now the doorlocation
 is DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL. But you may put it wherever you like. The
 datafile for the door with all the quotes in will be named after
 the name you give the door..

 Ex.
         DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL      <- door
         DOORS:WALL/SiLWALL.dat  <- datafile

 or..    DOORS:WALL.020          <- door
         DOORS:WALL.020.dat      <- datafile

 Don't forget to name the SiLWALL.info containing the config tooltypes
 to whatever you name the door.. If you are gonna use the SiLWALL.020
 file rename the DOORS/SiLWALL.info to DOORS/SiLWALL.020.info.
 Due to lack of time I have only implemented One tooltype yet.
 The next version, v3.00, will be Fully configurable.

 In the SilWALL.info there is a tooltype named CHEATMODE.
 The current setting is OFF. That means that if a User doesn't want
 to be anonymous his name will be printed after his quote in YELLOW
 color. That way nobody can 'cheat' and using the Anonymous option
 write another users handle in that place.
 But with CHEATMODE=ON the handles will be written the same color as
 the quotes which enables troublemakers to write shit and put another
 dudes handle in their place, can be quite amusing but if they start
 to write shit about the Sysop.. well :) you catch my drift!
 Check the 2 last quoted lines in the SiLWALL.iff picture to see
 what it looks like with or without CHEATMODE activated.
 Anyway that won't be a problem either in v3.00 wich will write the
 lines to the Callerslog, quite easy to fix but as I said, no time!!

 To launch this door from a bulletin file, ex BBS:Bull.txt then use
 the MCI Launch Door command ~CC_ like this...

  Ex:
          ---------------/STARTCUT/------
          ~
          ~CC_WALL
          ---------------/ENDCUT/--------
@endnode

@node "Package" "Contents of this package!"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "Main"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Contact"}

                       - Contents and Compability -

        This door can be used from Ami Express 1.1x up to /X 3.32+
     Though < 2.x users can't use the MCI command to launch the door!

 Files in This Package:

 BBS/Commands/BBSCmd/WALL.info    -CUSTOM COMMAND TOOLTYPES- 1068 bytes

 DOC/FILE_ID.DIZ                  -DESCRIPTION-               475 bytes
 DOC/SiLWALL.iff                  -WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE-       9088 bytes
 DOC/SiLWALL.GUIDE                -WHAT YOU ARE READING-     1518 bytes

 DOORS/SiLWALL.ANY                -680x0  VERSION-          20280 bytes
 DOORS/SiLWALL.020                -68020+ VERSION-          20280 bytes
 DOORS/SiLWALL.info               -CONFIG TOOLTYPES-         1068 bytes

    NOTE. The 680x0 Version is for Any amiga, be it 68000/20/30/40.
          The 68020 version is identical to the 030 compiled version
          so if you have a 030 use the 020+ version...
@endnode

